<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Banu Ghaniya of Ifriqiya</h1><p class="st-meta">1184 CE – 1233 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Almoravid family, which crossed from Majorca to wage a fifty-year war against the Almohads across Ifriqiya and the central Maghreb.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Banu Ghaniya, descendants of an Almoravid princess, held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a> as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banu-ghaniya-majorca">Banu Ghaniya Majorca</a> after the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a>. In 1184 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-ghaniya">Ali ibn Ghaniya</a> landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Bejaia</a>, seized the city from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> and opened a war to restore Almoravid rule, recognising the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>There was no fixed capital. The Banu Ghaniya fought as a roaming power, allied with Arab tribes such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-sulaym">Banu Sulaym</a> and, for a time, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharaf-al-din-qaraqush">Qaraqush</a>. Under Ali's brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yahya-ibn-ghaniya">Yahya ibn Ghaniya</a> they took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdia">Mahdia</a> around 1203, devastating towns and countryside across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tripolitania">Tripolitania</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Nasir retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdia">Mahdia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> in 1205 to 1206 and installed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafsid-dynasty">Hafsid</a> governor, whose successors kept up the fight. Yahya was driven into the desert and died in the 1230s, ending the movement. The chaos helped the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hafsid-sultanate">Hafsid Sultanate</a> emerge.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1184 CE – 1233 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.26%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1184 CE – 1233 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ali ibn Ghaniya, Yahya ibn Ghaniya</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (Maliki)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, <a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a>, <a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Banu Ghaniya, Almoravid remnant in Ifriqiya</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1208&amp;focus=banu-ghaniya-of-ifriqiya" aria-label="Banu Ghaniya of Ifriqiya on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4910 956 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Banu Ghaniya of Ifriqiya lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4794 1282h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5230 1212h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5230 1212h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Tunisia. <a href="/atlas?year=1208&amp;focus=banu-ghaniya-of-ifriqiya">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
